2026-10-19T04:58:05.8084265Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8095680Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8096420Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8096858Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8097064Z 
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8097353Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8097829Z 
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8098090Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8098528Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8098755Z 
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8098891Z If you would like to
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8099461Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8099906Z 
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8100305Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-19T04:58:05.8101002Z   $ sh ./install-nix
